preConditionHook:
// MICRO DOUBLE BOTTOM: this bar's low is within toleranceTicks of the low of
// the bar `gap` bars earlier. Short is the micro double top on the highs.
// Brooks: 'consecutive or nearly consecutive bars with identical or nearly
// identical lows'; 'most small bull reversals come from some type of micro
// double bottom'.
//
// ONE RULE WITH A `gap` PARAMETER: two sources state the adjacent-bar form
// (gap 1, the default) and two the one-bar-gap form (gap 2).
//
// THE TOLERANCE STAYS IN TICKS, not ATR: Brooks means literally identical or
// one-tick-apart extremes and all four sources say ticks. Tick division-first,
// toleranceTicks * (ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale()), computed once per bar
// into a local since both are per-symbol constants.
//
// T10-08's extra V-SHAPE conjunct -- low[1] above both matching lows, so the
// pair is a real dip rather than two bars of a slide -- is NOT carried: it only
// bites at gap >= 2 and it is a different rule, not a parameter of this one. Its
// close-up conjunct belongs to bar anatomy and is a separate placement.
//
// NOT Ledge, which counts bars matching the CURRENT bar's extreme anywhere
// inside a window; this requires the match at exactly `gap`. Not DoubleExtreme /
// DoubleExtremePullback, which pair CONFIRMED swing pivots at a variable
// distance with an ATR tolerance. The measured pivot sense (a flat run of equal
// extremes is ONE pivot) does not reach this rule, which uses no pivots at all.
//
// AbsValue is std::fabs per the translation table; <cmath> is already included
// by the emitter. Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a
// hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: gap.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
